      "title": "Carney says Trump tariffs upend decades-old US-Canada trade relationship",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/carney-says-trump-tariffs-upend-decades-old-us-canada-trade-relationship-126102200317_1.html",
      "description": "Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney said that US President Donald Trump's tariffs have driven up costs for American families and upended a decades-old trade relationship as he unveiled a multibillion-dollar plan to shield Canada's manufacturing heartland from the trade war.\nCarney on Wednesday also said he spoke with Trump for \"quite some time\" about issues including trade, as the US Embassy in Canada accused Canadian politicians of seeking to influence American politics ahead of next month's midterm elections.\nCarney and Ontario Premier Doug Ford rejected suggestions of improper interference.\nTrump has openly said he wants automakers to move production from Canada to the US, threatening an industry deeply integrated across the border for decades.\n\"US tariffs have upended a trade bargain that's existed for decades,\" Carney said. \"They've raised costs for American families while putting Ontario workers and businesses at a disadvantage and under a cloud of uncertainty.\"\nCarney said",
